# meta-deploy.list: the queue meta-deploy.bash runs, in this order.
#
# STANDING RULE (CLAUDE/AgentNotes.md): this list is exactly what needs running NOW. Add a
# run when it is pending, remove it once it has run and is done, leave out what cannot
# usefully run yet, then ask the owner to run meta-deploy.bash. Every step a run needs lives
# in the plan's own scripts, so this is the only command the owner is handed. The order is by
# dependency. A plan with none of triage.bash, deploy.bash and acceptance.bash has nothing
# for the script to do. A triage-only plan is run once, read-only. Words after the folder
# name are passed to that plan's triage.bash, both runs.
#
# One entry per line, three kinds:
#   <plan folder>                  its triage, deploy and acceptance scripts, in order
#   playbooks/<path>.yml           a change no plan owns; run as one unit through its own
#                                  shebang, which goes through run.bash, exactly as
#                                  ./playbooks/imports/<play>.yml does by hand
#   <plan folder>/<script>.bash    one plan script, for a step none of the three fixed names
#                                  fits; run as one unit, like a playbook entry
#
# A line starting with # is a comment and is the description of the entry below it: it is how
# the owner learns what a run will do, so write it. Blank lines are ignored. Any other line
# that is not an entry is a fatal error naming its line number.

# Plan 00201's UX fixes and security fixes: deploys the ccy launcher 3.98.10, which requires
# container 2.65, so the next ccy launch rebuilds the image once. In the envelope a human's
# accents, other scripts and emoji read as written; the agent's answer is an Element reply to
# the message, and Element shows the agent's avatar under each message it received; the skill
# and delivery frame carry the security rules (plugin 1.2.2). Rebuilds ccy-teams: Enter on a
# team row has "Open every team in Element, a window each"; a run that used sudo drops the
# credential before it exits, Ctrl-C included; the launch block names who can direct a
# session; a copied password serves one paste and is then gone. cc --teams gets the new deny
# rules and consent text. Running ccy sessions keep their old image until each is relaunched.
playbooks/imports/play-claude-yolo.yml
# Plan 00201's UX and security fixes: agent-bus-install software puts the same pingbus and kit
# in /usr/local/share/agent-bus/kit, so `cc --teams` sessions and LXC members get the same
# envelopes, replies, read receipts and security rules; and the agent-bus seat commands ccy and
# cc launch through, so a launch naming a stopped team says `ccy-teams apply <team>`, an
# unknown one lists the teams here, and `seat take` and `seat remove` end with `sudo -k`. No
# team, homeserver or firewall rule changes; every team then reads "out of date: software"
# until applied (ccy-teams offers it). The owner's checks are in Plan 00201's
# ACCEPTANCE-owner.md, from its "Morning start".
playbooks/imports/play-agent-bus.yml
